# Vibe Coder Workflow Rules

## Pre-Flight Checks
- Before generating substantial code, outline architecture, dependencies, and implementation slices.
- Confirm key constraints (runtime, data model, integration boundaries) before execution.
- Reject ambiguous prompts by requesting missing constraints instead of guessing.

## Focused Scoping
- Decompose large requests into 3-7 atomic subtasks with explicit outputs.
- Complete and verify each subtask before starting the next.
- Keep each subtask independently testable.

## Refactor for Clarity
- When code is complex or brittle, run a "refactor for clarity" pass:
  1) explain logic simply,
  2) rename opaque symbols,
  3) reduce branching complexity,
  4) highlight edge cases.

## Debug by Example
- For debugging, require:
  - failing snippet,
  - exact error message,
  - known-good reference snippet.
- Diff against the known-good example to isolate behavioral deviation before patching.

## Rollback and Re-Strategize
- If two consecutive fix attempts fail or broaden risk, revert to last known-good state and propose a revised approach.
- Prefer a smaller corrected implementation over a large speculative rewrite.
